    <briefdescription>
<para>Shout option condition. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A shout option is an option where the holder has the right to lock in a minimum value for the payoff at one (shout) time during the option&apos;s life. The minimum value is the option&apos;s intrinsic value at the shout time. </para>    </detaileddescription>
